-- The ORDERING control for the atom-guarantee seed: the envelope that carries it
-- must be built AFTER the effect-domain registry is populated.
--
-- `UserSlot` is exported ABSTRACTLY, so its constructor never reaches this module's
-- `registerVariants` and the only way `stash` can be accepted is the cross-module
-- seed (`deAtomsBefore`) -- exactly as in `xmod_abstract_wrapper_row_atoms`.  What
-- this row adds is a PARAMETERIZED label: `FileRead "x/*"` has a `Prefix` domain, so
-- the seeded atom's ⊤ parameter is read out of `driverState.effectDomains`.  Build
-- the envelope before that table is filled and every label reads back `PUnit`, the
-- guarantee stops matching the written row, and this `stash` is REJECTED with the
-- effect-variable laundering diagnostic -- an over-rejection, loud, on a program the
-- defining module accepts verbatim.
--
-- The direction matters both ways, which is why `plain` is here: the seed must
-- publish `UserSlot`'s ACTUAL guarantee, not "everything is guaranteed", so a relay
-- that supplies no `FileRead` at all still types as row-polymorphic rather than
-- silently acquiring the wrapper's row.
import w.{UserSlot, mkUserSlot}

stash : (Unit -> <FileRead "x/*" | e> Unit) -> UserSlot e
stash f = mkUserSlot f

reader : Unit -> <FileRead "x/*"> Unit
reader _ = ()

pureStash : UserSlot <>
pureStash = stash reader

main = println 1
